  "heading": "\\complex.numbers",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{the complex numbers}\\quad\\htmlClass{mlg-title-written}{\\mathbb{C}}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\complex.numbers]\nDefines: Cb ::= (C, 0, 1, +, *, -, /, i, neg(z_))\nabstractly:\nspecifies:\n. C is \\set\n. 0 \"in\" C\n. 1 \"in\" C\n. i \"in\" C\n. + is \\binary.operation:on{C}\n. * is \\binary.operation:on{C}\n. - is \\binary.operation:on{C}\n. / is \\binary.operation:on{C}\n. neg is \\function:on{C}:to{C}\nexpresses:\n. 0 != 1\n. i * i = -1\n. forAll: a, b, c \"in\" C\n  then:\n  . (a + b) + c = a + (b + c)\n  . a + b = b + a\n  . a + 0 = a\n  . (a * b) * c = a * (b * c)\n  . a * b = b * a\n  . a * 1 = a\n  . a * (b + c) = (a * b) + (a * c)\nEnables:\n. capability: z_ \"in\" Cb :-> z_ is \\complex\n. view:\n  as: S := C is \\set\nDocumented:\n. called: \"the complex numbers\"\n. written: \"\\mathbb{C}\"\n. description: \"The field of complex numbers\n                $\\mathbb{C} = \\mathbb{R}[i] / (i^2 + 1)$.\"\nId: \"19cb593a-f9c4-4ac8-82b7-2f32e590b67a\"",
